21892,"_gp_mult_vs_hist":false,"_score_mult_vs_hist":28.2,"_gate_fcf_yield":null,"_gp_fcf_yield":null,"_score_fcf_yield":null,"_gate_int_coverage":null,"_gp_int_coverage":null,"_score_int_coverage":null,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":-0.02531227920493781,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":73.6,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.09785750840314925,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":86.3,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.007136974125692641,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.1293606560736149,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":91.7,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08208144279299523,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":66.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03783889532742108,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":53.2,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.024858650043801833,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":81.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00762851486245137,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":87.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.22814,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"American Express Company, together with its subsidiaries, operates as an integrated payments company in the United States, Europe, the Middle East and Africa, the Asia Pacific, Australia, New Zealand, Latin America, Canada, the Caribbean, and internationally. It operates through four segments: U.S. Consumer Services, Commercial Services, International Card Services, and Global Merchant and Network Services. The company offers credit and charge cards and complementary products and services, including travel, dining, and lifestyle and expense management products and services; and banking and other payment and financing products and services, including deposits and non-card lending. It also provides merchant acquisition and processing, servicing and settlement, fraud prevention, and point-of-sale marketing and information products and services, as well as network services. The company offers its products and services to consumers, small businesses, mid-sized companies, and large corporations through mobile and online applications, affiliate marketing, customer referral programs, third-party service providers and business partners, in-house sales teams, direct mail, telephone, and direct response advertising. American Express Company was founded in 1850 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Stephen Joseph Squeri | Chairman & CEO | Age 65 | Compensation: $17.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 76K people. Revenue per employee of $940K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $208K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 18\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["American Express Company is a mega-cap financial services business with a $212.2B market cap on $72.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $16.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.70\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 23% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.014804129581832347},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $127.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["49 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is American Express (NYSE:AXP) Gaining Ground Despite The Pullback?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/financial/is-american-express-nyseaxp-gaining-ground-despite-the-pullback","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795801560.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.66,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"American Express Expects Another Year of 10% Revenue Growth. Prediction: The Stock Hits $400 in 2028.","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/american-express-expects-another-10-170502000.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795799548.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.751,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Pittsburg celebrates Small Business Saturday and art market","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/pittsburg-celebrates-small-business-saturday-212504000.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795820718.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.77,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Tybee Island preparing for Small Business Saturday","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/tybee-island-preparing-small-business-192320000.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795811600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.917,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Wall